{"name":"Shamanic Journey","hex":"#cc855a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shamanic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a shaman or to shamanism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shamanic"},{"term":"journey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set amount of travelling, seen as a single unit; a discrete trip, a voyage.","Any process or progression likened to a journey, especially one that involves difficulties or personal development."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel, to make a trip or voyage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shamanism","blocks":[{"text":"Shamanism is a spiritual practice that involves a practitioner (shaman) interacting with the spirit world through altered states of consciousness, such as trance. The goal of this is usually to direct spirits or spiritual energies into the physical world for the purpose of healing, divination, or to aid human beings in some other way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/SB_-_Altay_shaman_with_drum.jpg/330px-SB_-_Altay_shaman_with_drum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamanism","wikidata":"Q42042"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Witsen%27s_Shaman.JPG/500px-Witsen%27s_Shaman.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Witsen%27s_Shaman.JPG/500px-Witsen%27s_Shaman.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The earliest known depiction of a Siberian shaman, by the Dutch explorer Nicolaes Witsen, 17th century. Witsen called him a \"priest of the Devil\" and drew clawed feet for the supposed demonic qualities.[7]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWitsen's_Shaman.JPG"},{"sr